---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — PerkCommons"
  description="What information PerkCommons collects when people submit opportunities or report listings, and how that information is used."
>
  <section class="container py-14">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold">
      A plain-language privacy notice.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">
      PerkCommons collects limited information needed to operate the public directory,
      display approximate site activity counts, and moderate community submissions and listing reports.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Opportunity submissions</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          When you submit an opportunity, PerkCommons collects the information
          entered in the submission form. This may include an optional name or
          email address, details about the opportunity, and notes supplied for
          moderators.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          PerkCommons may also collect approximate geolocation, such as a
          country code derived from the request, together with technical
          request information used for moderation and abuse prevention. It
          does not ask for precise device GPS location.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Listing reports</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          When you report a listing, PerkCommons collects the report reason,
          any details you provide, the affected listing identifier, and an
          optional reporter email address. Similar approximate location and
          anti-abuse information may be processed to protect the reporting
          system from misuse.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">How the information is used</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Moderators use submitted information to review opportunities,
          investigate reports, contact a submitter or reporter when necessary,
          correct records, remove records, and protect the service from abuse.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What is public</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Published opportunity records are public. Optional submitter and
          reporter email addresses are not published. Approximate location and
          technical anti-abuse information associated with the person making a
          submission or report are not included in public opportunity records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Who controls the information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          PerkCommons is a free community-maintained project operated by Nataniel Bogacki,
          an individual based in Poland, not a registered company. For privacy enquiries,
          access or deletion requests, or to exercise your rights, contact
          <a href="mailto:privacy@perkcommons.com" class="font-medium underline">privacy@perkcommons.com</a>.
          You can use the directory without an account and without opting into analytics.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Optional first-party audience measurement</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          If you affirmatively accept optional analytics, your browser creates a random,
          pseudonymous ID in first-party local storage for the current UTC month.
          A Cloudflare Worker derives a keyed, month-specific cryptographic hash and sends
          it to an EU-restricted Cloudflare Durable Object. This lets us count participating
          browsers this month, participating browsers active during the previous five minutes,
          and deduplicated opportunity-page opens. These are approximate browser counts,
          not unique people or verified users. We use no third-party analytics pixels.
          The legal basis is your consent (GDPR Article 6(1)(a)); device storage and access
          for this optional purpose also require prior consent under Polish electronic
          communications law. Refusal has no effect on access to any PerkCommons feature.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Without consent, you can still see the public aggregate counters. We do not
          create an analytics ID or send activity events. Your consent or rejection is
          remembered only so we can honour your selection. You may change it at any time
          through the “Analytics choices” link in the footer. Consent is renewed after 180
          days or if the purpose changes. Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals
          prevent analytics participation even if you previously accepted.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Month-specific browser IDs are stored on your device while consent remains active.
          In the EU counter store, hashed current-month identifiers are deleted after the
          month changes, active-presence records expire after five minutes, and
          per-listing duplicate-suppression records expire after 30 minutes.
          Cumulative listing totals are retained in aggregate without browser identifiers.
          We process IP addresses temporarily at Cloudflare to limit abusive submissions
          to this counter endpoint, but do not place raw IP addresses in the counter database.
          Withdrawing consent deletes the local analytics ID and requests deletion of the
          associated current-month hashed records; if offline, the deletion request is
          retried the next time you use the site. Aggregate totals cannot be attributed to
          or removed for an individual browser.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
          <button type="button" data-open-analytics-settings class="min-h-11 rounded-md border border-line bg-surface px-4 font-medium text-ink">Change analytics choices</button>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted" role="status">Your current analytics preference is shown in the choice panel.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Other processing and lawful bases</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Submissions, corrections and reports are processed for the legitimate interests
          of maintaining a safe, accurate public directory and responding to community
          requests (GDPR Article 6(1)(f)). Information you voluntarily provide may
          include contact details and evidence. Access to moderation records is restricted;
          project moderation, security and retention policies explain operational handling.
          We use necessary technical information to deliver the website and protect it
          from abuse. We do not sell visitor information or use it to target ads.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Processors and international transfers</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          We use Cloudflare to serve the site, process requests and store optional
          analytics aggregates. Analytics Durable Object storage is restricted to
          the European Union, but this does not guarantee all Cloudflare edge
          processing, technical metadata or logs remain there. We use Supabase
          for private submissions and moderation. These providers may involve
          processing outside the European Economic Area subject to applicable
          contractual and legal safeguards, including standard contractual
          clauses where required. Cloudflare publishes its
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-customer-dpa/" class="underline">Data Processing Addendum</a>.
          Contact us for further information about the safeguards relevant to your data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Your data rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Depending on the circumstances, you may request access, correction, erasure,
          restriction, portability or objection to personal-data processing. You can
          withdraw analytics consent at any time without affecting the lawfulness of
          earlier processing. If you no longer hold the random ID, we may be unable
          to link an otherwise pseudonymous counter record to you; we do not collect
          additional identity information solely to identify anonymous-looking statistics.
          To make a request, email <a href="mailto:privacy@perkcommons.com" class="underline">privacy@perkcommons.com</a>.
          You may also complain to the Polish supervisory authority,
          <a href="https://uodo.gov.pl/" class="underline">Urząd Ochrony Danych Osobowych (UODO)</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-line pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">
          Questions or privacy concerns can be sent to
          <a class="font-medium" href="mailto:privacy@perkcommons.com">privacy@perkcommons.com</a>.
          General reports can also be sent to
          <a class="font-medium" href="mailto:hello@perkcommons.com">hello@perkcommons.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
